# Update docs before commit

After **`pnpm check`** passes (and **`pnpm build`** when [validate-commit-push.mdc](validate-commit-push.mdc) requires it), and **before** **`git commit`**, confirm documentation **and** the roadmap PM board match what you are about to ship.

## Keep CHANGELOG up to date

**[`doc/CHANGELOG.md`](../../doc/CHANGELOG.md) must stay current** with shipped user-facing work. Treat a stale **[Unreleased]** section as a blocker for commit — same as a failing test.

- **When:** any user-visible feature, fix, default change, permission/network change, or settings/UI copy that affects what people see or do.
- **Where:** append under **[Unreleased]** in **Added**, **Changed**, or **Fixed** ([Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/) style).
- **How:** plain language about what users notice — not commit hashes, file paths, or internal refactors.
- **Scope:** major/minor lines only (see the header in `CHANGELOG.md`); patch detail stays in Git history.
- **Same commit:** stage CHANGELOG updates **with** the code they describe whenever possible; do not leave **[Unreleased]** empty while landing meaningful extension changes.
- **Settings embed:** when **[Unreleased]** (or rolled history) should appear in **Settings > Changelog**, regenerate with **`pnpm generate:settings-changelog`** ([settings-changelog-version-bump.mdc](settings-changelog-version-bump.mdc)).

When unsure whether something is user-facing, add a short **[Unreleased]** line rather than ship silent product changes.

## Keep the PM board current (major / roadmap work)

After **major** shipped work — new features, completing or advancing a roadmap item, multi-file product changes, or anything that closes/moves a `pm:PM-T###` task — update the Projocalypse plan in the **same delivery**:

1. Edit [`doc/PLAN/ROADMAP-PM-BOARD.md`](../../doc/PLAN/ROADMAP-PM-BOARD.md) — check `[x]` / move `pm:section=Done` (or the correct sprint column) for finished ids; add approved items from [`ROADMAP.md`](../../doc/PLAN/ROADMAP.md) only with maintainer intent.
2. Run **`pnpm pm:sync`** so `.projocalypse/pending/tabocalypse-roadmap.json` matches the plan.
3. Run **`pnpm pm:stale`** and fix drift if reported.
4. Stage **plan + pending JSON** with the feature/fix (or an immediate follow-up commit in the same PR).

**Skip PM board** only when the change is unrelated to roadmap items (typo, pure test/tooling, internal refactor with no product milestone). Prefer a quick glance at `ROADMAP-PM-BOARD.md` over silent skip when unsure.

Full sync loop: [tabocalypse-pm-board.mdc](tabocalypse-pm-board.mdc) and skill **`tabocalypse-pm-board`**.

## When to update other docs

| Change | Update |
| --- | --- |
| User-facing feature, fix, or default | **[Unreleased]** in [`doc/CHANGELOG.md`](../../doc/CHANGELOG.md) (required — see above) |
| Completes / advances a roadmap `pm:PM-T###` or major milestone | [`ROADMAP-PM-BOARD.md`](../../doc/PLAN/ROADMAP-PM-BOARD.md) + **`pnpm pm:sync`** (required — see above) |
| Permissions, `host_permissions`, manifest, or network use | [`PRIVACY.md`](../../PRIVACY.md); [`doc/STORE-LISTING.md`](../../doc/STORE-LISTING.md) / [`doc/PUBLISHING-EXTENSION-STORES.md`](../../doc/PUBLISHING-EXTENSION-STORES.md) when store copy or justifications change |
| New or renamed `doc/*.md` guide | Root [`README.md`](../../README.md) Documentation section + [`doc/README.md`](../../doc/README.md) index ([documentation-layout.mdc](documentation-layout.mdc)) |
| Supported browsers, install steps, or WXT output paths | Relevant `doc/*`, [`README.md`](../../README.md); keep Safari with Chrome, Edge, Firefox ([safari-supported-browser.mdc](safari-supported-browser.mdc)) |
| Settings paths, widget labels, or first-run copy | Matching doc section + CHANGELOG when user-visible ([user-facing-copy.mdc](user-facing-copy.mdc)) |

## When to skip

- Internal refactors with **no** shipped behavior, permissions, network, or roadmap status change
- Test-only, tooling-only, or agent-only edits (`.cursor/`, CI internals) with no product impact — except when the edit **is** the docs/PM rule itself
- Trivial typo in a non-shipped comment

Use judgment on other docs; **CHANGELOG is never optional** for user-facing shipped work. **PM board sync is never optional** when a roadmap task status should change.

## Workflow order

```
pnpm check → (pnpm build when needed) → CHANGELOG [Unreleased] → PM board + pnpm pm:sync (if major/roadmap) → stage docs/pending → git commit
```

Do **not** commit meaningful shipped work when checks are green but **[Unreleased]** in `doc/CHANGELOG.md` is stale, or a finished `pm:PM-T###` is still unchecked on the board.

## Commit pairing

- Prefer **one commit** that includes code + CHANGELOG + PM plan/pending when they describe the same change.
- A **docs/PM-only follow-up** is fine when catching up after an earlier code commit — still run **`pnpm check`** (and **`pnpm pm:stale`** if the plan changed) before that commit.
